  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0388, and it contains seven tables. The tables are:\n1. Supplier_Table: This table stores information about suppliers, including their ID, information, relationship management, and update time. The primary key is Supplier_ID, and the columns are Creation_Time, Supplier_ID, Supplier_Information, Supplier_Relationship_Management, and Update_Time.\n2. Project_Table: This table stores information about projects, including their ID, information, progress management, and update time. The primary key is Project_ID, and the columns are Creation_Time, Project_ID, Project_Information, Project_Progress_Management, and Update_Time.\n3. Salary_Table: This table stores information about salaries, including their calculation, distribution, ID, and update time. The primary key is Salary_ID, and the columns are Creation_Time, Salary_Calculation, Salary_Distribution, Salary_ID, and Update_Time.\n4. Supplier_Supply_Project: This table stores information about the relationship between suppliers and projects, including the supplier ID and project ID. The primary key is a composite key of Supplier_ID and Project_ID, and the columns are Project_ID, Supplier_ID, and Update_Time.\n5. Employee_Table: This table stores information about employees, including their ID, information, performance evaluation, position allocation, salary ID, and update time. The primary key is Employee_ID, and the columns are Creation_Time, Employee_ID, Employee_Information, Performance_Evaluation, Position_Allocation, Salary_ID, Update_Time.\n6. Attendance_Record_Table: This table stores information about attendance records, including the attendance ID, record, creation time, employee ID, employee punch-in time, update time, and employee ID. The primary key is Attendance_ID, and the columns are Attendance_ID, Attendance_Record, Creation_Time, Employee_ID, Employee_Punch_In, Update_Time.\n7. Employee_Project_Allocation: This table stores information about the allocation of employees to projects, including the employee ID and project ID. The primary key is a composite key of Employee_ID and Project_ID, and the columns are Employee_ID, Project_ID, and Update_Time.\nEach table has its own set of columns, and some of the columns are foreign keys that reference other tables. For example, the Supplier_Supply_Project table has foreign keys to the Supplier_Table and Project_Table, while the Employee_Table has a foreign key to the Salary_Table. The tables also have primary keys and unique constraints to ensure data integrity.",
  "gold_question": "The requirements analysis of a certain enterprise management system is as follows:\n1. Employee management: including employee information, job assignment, performance appraisal, salary number, creation time, update time, etc. An employee can participate in multiple projects.\n2. Supplier management: including supplier information, supplier relationship management, creation time, update time, etc. A supplier can supply multiple projects.\n3. Project management: including project information, project progress management, creation time, update time, etc. A project contains multiple employees and can have multiple suppliers.\n4. Attendance management: including employee number, employee clock-in, attendance record, creation time, update time, etc.\n5. Salary management: including salary payment, salary calculation, creation time, update time, etc.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0388.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0388\nCREATE TABLE `supplier_table` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `supplier_relationship_management` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_table` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_progress_management` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `salary_table` (\n  `salary_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `salary_calculation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary_distribution` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`salary_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supplier_supply_project` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`, `project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `supplier_supply_project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supplier_id`) REFERENCES `supplier_table` (`supplier_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `supplier_supply_project_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project_table` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_table` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `performance_evaluation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position_allocation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`salary_id`) REFERENCES `salary_table` (`salary_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attendance_record_table` (\n  `attendance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attendance_record` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_punch_in` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`attendance_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_record_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee_table` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_project_allocation` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_project_allocation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee_table` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_project_allocation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project_table` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
